WEBVTT

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:08.170
The vast ocean of words.

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:18.020
Without a means to cross the ocean,

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:21.150
we can only stand and watch,

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:28.800
keeping the words inside
we desperately want to express.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:36.100
A dictionary is a ship that is able
to cross that ocean.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:58.660
A quiet dreamlike morning, the madder red sky
shines through the window and reflects on my pen

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:04.800
The vivid clatter of the night,
I wander between cities like a cat

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:11.440
Deep thoughts, flexible conception;
foreseeable aspirations, distant memories; unruly hair

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:18.080
Narrow mind, large circle of friends;
long silence, short greeting;tone of voice

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:24.380
The light in our eyes that differ from each other,
traces of friendship that’s not in the treaty

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:30.690
In the ocean that sweeps the sand of eternity

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:37.660
Swept and sunk in the waves with sparse
opposites and similarities

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:44.170
Clashing and exact opposites become
resolved and connected

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:50.710
Reference, conclusion; I’ll gather words that have
scattered over many months and years

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:57.180
The fragrant sea breeze;
the connection that rests on the seashore, become one.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:10.830
Vastness

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:18.910
What was the first dictionary you held,
Matsumoto-sensei?

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:21.440
It was Fumihiko Otsuki's
Genkai, A Sea of Words,

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:23.910
which I inherited from my grandfather.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.850
When I learned that Otsuki compiled it
by himself

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.250
after overcoming many obstacles,

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:33.220
it left a deep impression on me
as a child.

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:37.690
I bet you looked up
some naughty words too.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:40.530
I would never.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.160
Is that right?

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:45.930
My first dictionary was the Iwanami
Japanese Dictionary in junior high.

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:48.770
I looked up all the dirty words.

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:52.570
But that is a very elegant
and refined dictionary.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:54.810
I'm sure you were only disappointed.

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:56.810
Yes, that's exactly right.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:00.650
Hey, it sounds like
you looked them up too.

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:08.590
We've made many dictionaries together,
Araki.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:10.660
I have fond memories of each.

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:19.900
I'm so sorry that I won't be able
to see our work through to the end.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:24.240
So you will not be able to stay on
in the editorial department?

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:27.710
I do plan to drop by as much as I can,

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.980
but my wife's condition isn't improving.

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:34.480
I've been too busy with the dictionaries
to do anything for her,

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:37.950
so I wanted to at least be by her side
after retirement.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:39.650
That is probably for the best.

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:43.560
It is your turn to support her now.

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:53.530
I promise to find my successor
before I retire.

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:55.870
Someone who will be able
to perfectly assist you,

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.900
lead the dictionary's
editorial department,

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:03.280
and further advance our plans
to create a new dictionary.

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:05.380
Someone young and brilliant.

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:12.390
I doubt I will ever meet another editor
like you.

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:15.390
Compiling a dictionary
is very specialized.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:18.790
It's completely different from books
and magazines.

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:21.660
It requires patience
and attention to detail,

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:24.500
an indulgence for words
but not overly so,

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.870
while also having a wide perspective.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:31.370
Is there a young person like that
in this day and age?

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:35.010
There has to be.

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:39.480
I will do whatever I have to do
to find one.

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:51.020
"Dictionary Editorial Department"

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:53.080
Sasaki-san, where's Nishioka?

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:55.010
He's not back yet.

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:57.650
Where has he gone off to again?

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:01.820
-Sasaki-san, I have a favor to ask.
-Yes?

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:05.190
If there is anybody who might be suitable
for dictionary editing--

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:09.060
I don't care what department they're in.
--would you let me know?

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:11.490
Okay.

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:16.570
It is absolutely crucial
in order to create our Daitokai.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:35.150
"Jinbou-cho Station"

00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:43.530
My name is Mitsuya Majime,
from Genbu Books Publishing.

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:48.130
I want to express our gratitude
for carrying our latest issues in your store.

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:53.140
I have brought some sales-promotion
material with me today.

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:57.170
I'm sorry, could we take this over there
since this is the register here?

00:05:57.510 --> 00:05:59.140
Of course.

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:01.280
Here, sir.

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:03.680
We would be honored
if you would use this.

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:06.550
Yes, thank you very much.

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:09.190
Well, I have this now, so...

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:10.990
Thank you very much!

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:13.260
Yes, yes. Good day, then.

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:15.960
Have a good day.

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:17.930
Welcome.

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:20.530
That will be 680 yen.

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:24.930
Um, who did that man say
he worked for?

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:26.740
Genbu Books Publishing.

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:29.070
I'm sorry he startled you.

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:30.810
No, I am sorry.

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:36.180
I apologize for our salesman's behavior.

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:39.850
I promise I will have a word with him.

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:45.050
We hope to continue our business
with you, as you are a valued customer.

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:48.190
Yes, of course.
Thank you for your courteous gesture.

00:06:51.290 --> 00:06:54.760
Man, I don't remember a guy like that
in our sales department.

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:57.170
Wait, he's gone already.

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:00.640
Wait! Stop there, sales guy!

00:07:04.810 --> 00:07:06.580
Yeah, you!

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:12.110
You are from
the dictionary editorial department?

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:14.650
I did not realize
you were also from Genbu Books Publishing.

00:07:15.220 --> 00:07:16.320
I am very sorry.

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:19.660
No, that's what I'm trying to say.

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:24.190
If you carry around a bag
from their rival store during sales call,

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:26.900
they wouldn't take you serious.

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:30.600
Oh, I just liked the color and look of it.

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:32.270
But that's not the point.

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:38.270
In order for every bookstore
to feel comfortable selling our products,

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:42.280
you always have to put yourself
in their position.

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:45.380
That's like Sales 101.

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:50.320
Do you understand,
um, Mitsuya Majime?

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:52.220
Yes, I'm Majime.

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:54.320
Majime, huh?

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:57.760
Look, it's good that you're an earnest,
hardworking guy.

00:07:57.890 --> 00:08:00.230
I'm just saying
"read the air" a little more.

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:01.900
Air?

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:03.670
What?

00:08:04.070 --> 00:08:06.370
"To read the air."

00:08:06.700 --> 00:08:10.710
The air you are referring to
is not breathed.

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:14.940
You are using it to mean a situation
or mood.

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:16.110
Is that right?

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:21.350
You can also use it as "the air is heavy."

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:27.390
Which would mean an uncomfortable
situation that you would want to leave.

00:08:27.720 --> 00:08:31.390
Hey, I'm feeling that right now.

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:34.000
Well, keep at it.

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:37.100
Um...

00:08:38.070 --> 00:08:41.000
Thank you for your lesson.

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:43.970
Sure.

00:09:02.090 --> 00:09:03.830
Souunsou

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:05.130
I have returned.

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:38.030
Tora-san.

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:43.200
I have to make dinner, don't I?

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:47.100
Tora-san, I hope dried sardines
are okay with you.

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:59.880
Micchan? Are you back?

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:03.350
Yes, I just got in now.

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:06.060
I made too much food.

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:08.760
Would you like some?

00:10:08.890 --> 00:10:10.330
Thank you.

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:12.930
I will take you up on your offer.

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:17.000
Thank you for the meal.

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:21.500
I have these too.

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:24.010
Oh, they smell very nice.

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:27.480
It's Inosaka Meat's proud new addition.

00:10:28.280 --> 00:10:31.480
He said he would give a discount
this week to get people to try them,

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:33.520
so I bought enough for two.

00:10:33.850 --> 00:10:37.990
I see.
It does smell a little different from usual.

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:40.820
You know what Old Man Inosaka
told his son?

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:44.030
He said, "We have to change.

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:46.430
We need to come up
with something new."

00:10:46.560 --> 00:10:48.360
Can you believe that?

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:51.230
He's apparently very enthusiastic.

00:10:51.370 --> 00:10:53.200
They have to change.

00:10:56.570 --> 00:11:01.180
Oh, I've noticed you've added
to your pile of books.

00:11:01.310 --> 00:11:03.580
I'm so sorry. Were they in the way?

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:08.180
I thought I organized them
so they wouldn't spill out into the hallway.

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:10.920
Don't worry about it.

00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:13.160
I just got a glimpse from the hallway.

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:16.060
Souunsou's floors can take it.

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:18.490
You can pile on even more.

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:24.400
I mean, if a bookworm like you
stop buying books,

00:11:24.970 --> 00:11:27.500
I'd be even more worried.

00:11:28.900 --> 00:11:30.970
That is a relief to hear you say.

00:11:57.870 --> 00:11:59.400
Words.

00:11:59.540 --> 00:12:02.400
Words as vast as the ocean.

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:04.640
Unable to express my feelings

00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:07.440
or know which direction to head,

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:09.610
I sink into the ocean.

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:13.620
The ocean swallows me.

00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:16.620
Someone please reach out to me.

00:12:17.650 --> 00:12:20.560
Show me the way.

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:42.890
-Hey, he's here again?
-Who is?

00:12:43.020 --> 00:12:45.490
Araki-san
from the dictionary editorial department.

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:48.530
-Dictionary?
-Apparently he's looking for talent.

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:52.000
Seriously?
Well, I'd better keep my head down, then.

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:54.500
There has to be someone.

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:37.110
It requires patience
and attention to detail,

00:13:37.240 --> 00:13:40.810
an indulgence for words
but not overly so,

00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:43.620
while also having a wide perspective.

00:13:44.020 --> 00:13:46.520
Someone like that has to exist.

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:48.220
They have to.

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:50.220
"Dictionary Editorial Department"

00:13:54.190 --> 00:13:56.000
Araki-san.

00:13:56.660 --> 00:13:58.300
Did you skip lunch today?

00:13:58.630 --> 00:14:00.170
I don't have time for lunch.

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:03.100
I wish I could be as carefree as you.

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:04.770
That's not very nice.

00:14:04.910 --> 00:14:06.710
I looked too, you know.

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:08.910
Right, Sasaki-san?

00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:11.750
But finding someone suited
for making dictionaries

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:14.150
isn't going to be very easy.

00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:15.580
Pathetic.

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:18.220
The company is neglecting dictionaries.

00:14:18.550 --> 00:14:19.990
Can you blame them?

00:14:20.120 --> 00:14:24.760
Making dictionaries requires
an enormous amount of money and time.

00:14:24.890 --> 00:14:27.290
-Enormous.
-And business has been bad.

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:31.030
Everyone is only interested in things
that will sell quickly.

00:14:31.160 --> 00:14:32.930
Dictionaries have a good image

00:14:33.070 --> 00:14:35.670
and are generally resilient in the market.

00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:38.610
This is precisely why
we need to stay motivated

00:14:38.740 --> 00:14:40.970
and look toward the future.

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:43.740
I mean,
there are so many dictionaries already.

00:14:43.880 --> 00:14:44.910
Hey.

00:14:45.050 --> 00:14:46.780
As an dictionary editor,

00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:49.720
I hope you don't believe
that all dictionaries are the same.

00:14:49.850 --> 00:14:51.080
No. Even I know.

00:14:51.220 --> 00:14:53.950
Considering word interpretation
and the selection process,

00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:55.990
each dictionary has its own personality.

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:58.220
No two dictionaries are the same.

00:14:58.890 --> 00:15:01.330
We are going to make a new dictionary

00:15:01.660 --> 00:15:04.900
befitting the future
with Matsumoto-sensei.

00:15:05.030 --> 00:15:06.900
Even I understand that.

00:15:07.030 --> 00:15:12.710
But there aren't very many employees
here who are as excellent as I am.

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:16.340
Even yesterday,
I ran into some guy in Sales on the street.

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:17.910
You won't believe it.

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:20.610
I bet he was just obsessed
with sales figures.

00:15:20.750 --> 00:15:22.620
No, almost the opposite.

00:15:22.750 --> 00:15:27.120
Guy's not cut out for sales at all.
I gave him a stern talking-to.

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:29.920
Air?

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:32.290
"To read the air."

00:15:32.630 --> 00:15:34.230
It is not breathed.

00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:39.970
You are using "air" to mean
a situation or mood.

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:41.800
Is that right?

00:15:43.070 --> 00:15:45.040
What else was there?

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:48.240
He said something
about uncomfortable situations

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:50.380
and wanting to leave
where you're standing.

00:15:50.710 --> 00:15:54.210
Did he just come up with that
on the spot?

00:15:54.350 --> 00:15:56.720
That's an interesting salesman.

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:58.350
Sounds like he has a knack for it.

00:15:58.690 --> 00:16:01.790
What? I swear you'd cringe if you met him,
Sasaki-san.

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:04.990
He seriously can't read the air.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:07.060
-I'll meet him.
-What?

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:08.800
What was his name?

00:16:08.930 --> 00:16:11.770
-I can't wait. You come with me.
-What?

00:16:12.730 --> 00:16:16.740
Wait, hold on, Araki-san.

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:20.670
He was able to come up
with multiple definitions instantaneously.

00:16:21.140 --> 00:16:25.080
That's a crucial ability to have
when writing a dictionary.

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:27.780
Seriously,
there's no point in meeting him.

00:16:27.910 --> 00:16:29.980
He's really stupidly earnest
and an airhead.

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:31.920
Oh, this is him.

00:16:34.390 --> 00:16:37.990
Sale Department (I), Majime.

00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:39.260
Let's go.

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:40.890
"Sales Department (I)"

00:17:02.150 --> 00:17:04.220
Compiling a dictionary
is very specialized.

00:17:04.350 --> 00:17:09.420
It's completely different from books
and magazines.

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:14.190
Invoices, Sales History, Asset Values

00:17:14.330 --> 00:17:16.730
"New Published Book Distribution List"

00:17:28.510 --> 00:17:31.480
"Financial Statement"

00:17:39.350 --> 00:17:42.860
It requires patience
and attention to detail,

00:17:42.990 --> 00:17:46.860
an indulgence for words
but not overly so,

00:17:46.990 --> 00:17:50.360
while also having a wide perspective.

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:56.500
Is there a young person like that
in this day and age?

00:18:06.910 --> 00:18:07.910
Kouhei Araki
Dictionary Editorial Department

00:18:08.050 --> 00:18:10.520
I'm Araki,
with the dictionary editorial department.

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:15.220
I'm Majime,
with the Sales Department (I).

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:17.390
That is a very unusual last name
you have.

00:18:17.520 --> 00:18:19.230
Where are you from?

00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:21.130
I'm from Tokyo,

00:18:21.260 --> 00:18:23.360
but both of my parents
are from Wakayama.

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:26.570
Apparently the old tonya stores
were also referred to as majimes.

00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:31.500
I see, so it comes from making
arrangements for the traveler's horse.

00:18:32.440 --> 00:18:34.540
Oh, I'm sorry to go off on a tangent.

00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:36.040
No, that's not a problem.

00:18:36.180 --> 00:18:38.480
I've been asked about the origins
of my name before,

00:18:38.810 --> 00:18:41.550
but this is the first time
someone's written it down.

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:46.550
What would you do
if you were asked to explain "right"?

00:18:47.590 --> 00:18:48.590
"Right"?

00:18:49.360 --> 00:18:53.560
Do you mean the direction
or the ideology?

00:18:53.890 --> 00:18:55.360
"Right" as in the direction.

00:19:02.040 --> 00:19:04.840
If I were to say
the side you hold your chopsticks with,

00:19:04.970 --> 00:19:07.370
it would ignore those
who are left-handed.

00:19:07.510 --> 00:19:10.080
And if I say it's the side
your heart isn't on,

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:13.580
there are actually people
who have their hearts on the right.

00:19:15.010 --> 00:19:17.050
When you face your body north,

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:19.590
it is the side that is on the east side.

00:19:21.150 --> 00:19:23.620
Then how would you convey "island"?

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:26.990
Do you mean the land mass,
anatomical term, or abstractly?

00:19:27.130 --> 00:19:28.560
The land mass.

00:19:28.900 --> 00:19:33.930
A comparatively small land mass
surrounded by water, perhaps?

00:19:34.070 --> 00:19:36.100
No, that's not enough.

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:40.070
Enoshima is still an island
while having a portion connected to land,

00:19:40.210 --> 00:19:41.240
which means...

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:43.210
It's okay, I've heard enough.

00:19:44.880 --> 00:19:48.380
Majime, I would like to use your talents
to create Daitokai,

00:19:48.510 --> 00:19:51.050
to create a new dictionary with us.

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:53.390
You're kidding, right?

00:19:56.390 --> 00:19:58.120
A dictionary?

00:20:03.600 --> 00:20:06.270
Those who stand
in front of an ocean of words

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:10.200
in order to carry their hearts
and feelings,

00:20:11.240 --> 00:20:14.610
we create a ship.

00:20:15.510 --> 00:20:21.450
A ship called the Daitokai
to cross the ocean of words.

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:28.190
VASTNESS: of very great area or extent; immense.

00:20:32.630 --> 00:20:43.140
Hey, it’s a full moon tonight

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:54.150
I speak to you softly as you sleep

00:20:55.520 --> 00:21:05.990
Your gestures, attitude, and way of life

00:21:06.460 --> 00:21:12.700
Mean so much to me more than any word

00:21:13.030 --> 00:21:18.540
So please stay the way you are

00:21:19.270 --> 00:21:24.640
I & I = You & I
Feel it

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:30.120
Here with you, forever by your side

00:21:30.280 --> 00:21:43.030
I’ve loved you from the day we met

00:21:51.740 --> 00:21:53.740
I memorized every single line.

00:21:54.170 --> 00:21:55.710
Relax, relax...

00:21:56.210 --> 00:21:58.010
Rerax...Oops!

00:22:02.180 --> 00:22:03.050
Oh no...

00:22:03.580 --> 00:22:06.120
The line I memorized has all gone...
